This position has a selective placement factor that will be used to screen out ineligible candidates. The selective placement factor is: You must currently be a licensed Professional Engineer (PE) if applying for the 0801 series. You must be a Registered Architect (RA) if applying for the 0808 series. Your license or registration must be held in a State, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, or a territory of the United States. Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-12 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1. Performs all aspects of landscape architectural design for a wide variety of installation shore facility projects and sites, including planning, concept design development, sustainable design, design analyses, compliance with codes and standards, drawings, specifications, cost estimates, and other required services;
2. Participates in multi-disciplinary in-house design teams; 3. Provides day-to-day expert technical guidance and support in developing initial project documents plans, specifications, studies, reports, and other design work products;
4. Prepares landscape architecture design, construction documents and specifications, for new and renovation projects to various types of Navy and Marine Corps facilities, using the latest technological design and drafting tools (CAD);
5. Performs technical management and oversight on execution of multi-disciplinary design projects; 6. Coordinates the landscape architectural design with the architectural and engineering disciplines for Design-Bid-Build (DBB) and Design-Build (DB) projects to ensure overall compatibility and efficiency of the site and building design; 7. Provides expert technical advice and direction, review and administration related to the planning, design, construction, testing, operation, maintenance and repairs for new and existing naval shore facilities; 8. Provides technical landscape architectural training and mentoring for new and junior employees to increase their technical competency; 9. Provides post construction award services (PCAS), including review and approval of contractor's submittals for conformance with the requirements of the contract drawings and specifications; 10. Provides technical guidance to A/E firms regarding criteria application and unique DoD functional requirements; 11. Presents design and/or studies to higher level authorities or other Components within NAVFAC, and to Supported Commanders and other stakeholders, as required. Ensures the in-house landscape design is complete, timely, and quality design work product and; 12. Provides a high degree of innovation, creativity, imagination, resourcefulness and technical judgment concerning design, construction, and contractual problems without precedent. NOTE: This information must be supported in your resume to be considered for this position. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
